  "final_answer": "Cause: load_config did a shallow copy of DEFAULTS (dict(DEFAULTS)), so nested dicts and lists such as logging.handlers and allowed_hosts were shared with the module-level defaults. enable_debug() mutated them in place, so later configs inherited the debug changes. merge() also stored override lists/dicts by reference, so returned configs could alias caller data.\n\nFix: loader.py now uses copy.deepcopy(DEFAULTS), and merge.py deep-copies values taken from the override. The existing 4 tests pass. I did not add a regression test for the leak.",
